### recall.select - Collections (one-to-one: user+project <-> Qdrant collection)
# Self-contained: creates a user and project, then provisions the collection.
# Registering also creates the backing Qdrant collection named rs_{userId}_{projectId}.
# (JetBrains HTTP client format.)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Setup: create a user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "collections@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("userId", response.body.id);
%}

### Setup: create a project
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "default"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("projectId", response.body.id);
%}

### Register the collection -> 201, name = rs_{userId}_{projectId}, counters at 0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/collection

### Re-register is idempotent -> returns the same record (no duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/collection

### Get the collection (shows points_count / calls_count for stats & limits)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/collection

### Delete the collection -> 204 (drops both the Mongo record and Qdrant collection)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/collection
